<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
    <div class="hero bg-base-200 py-12 px-8 rounded-box">
      <div class="hero-content flex-col lg:flex-row gap-12">
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center shrink-0">
          <div class="avatar">
            <div class="w-64 rounded-full ring ring-base-300 ring-offset-base-100 ring-offset-2 overflow-hidden">
              <img alt="me on my last year in Japan" src={~p"/images/fall_tree.jpg"} />
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1 text-base-content/70">Bioinformatician, cloud advocate, food nerd</p>
          <div class="mt-4 flex gap-4">
            <.link
              href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jfortizq"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              aria-label="LinkedIn profile"
              class="text-base-content/80 hover:text-primary transition-colors"
            >
              <.devicon name="linkedin" class="size-8" />
            </.link>
            <.link
              href="https://github.com/biofilos"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              aria-label="GitHub profile"
              class="text-white hover:text-primary transition-colors"
            >
              <.devicon name="github" class="size-8" />
            </.link>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="max-w-2xl">
          <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold">Nice, to meet you!</h1>
          <p class="pt-6 text-xl leading-relaxed">
            Hi, I'm Juan Felipe, a bioinformatician who loves digging into the code of life.
          </p>
          <p class="pt-4 text-xl leading-relaxed">
            Whether it's unraveling the mysteries of evolution, harnessing the power of cloud computing for genomic analysis, or experimenting with the latest data visualization techniques, I'm passionate about pushing boundaries and finding creative solutions to questions, problems, and puzzles.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold pt-8 pb-4">Background</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <.milestone_card
        image={~p"/images/unal_green.jpg"}
        image_alt="Jardín Botánico de San Andrés, Universidad Nacional de Colombia"
        title="BSc. Biology"
        subtitle="U. Nacional. Colombia"
      >
        As part of my thesis for Biology at the <.link
          href="https://unal.edu.co"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
        >National University of Colombia</.link>, I started my career working on drift algae
        and their taxonomy. Then I joined Manihot Biotec, lab specialized in plant immunity.
        There, I learned about bioinformatics, genome annotation, molecular modelling,
        and phylogenetics.
      </.milestone_card>
      <.milestone_card
        image={~p"/images/laramie.jpg"}
        image_alt="At Vedawoo park"
        title="MSc. Molecular Biology"
        subtitle="U. Wyoming. USA"
      >
        For my Masters degree in Molecular Biology at the <.link
          href="www.uwyo.edu"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
        >University of Wyoming</.link>, I wrote my first program, which was used to analyze how the intrinsic protein disorder in
        flavivirus proteins has a clear phylogenetic signal.
      </.milestone_card>
      <.milestone_card
        image={~p"/images/vandy_cooking.png"}
        image_alt="Teaching how to make delicious Colombian food to my friends at the uni"
        title="PhD. Biological Sciences"
        subtitle="Vanderbilt U. USA"
      >
        In my PhD for Biological Sciences at the
        <.link
          href="https://as.vanderbilt.edu/rokaslab/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
        >
          Rokas Lab
        </.link>
        at <.link
          href="https://vanderbilt.edu"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
        >Vanderbilt University</.link>, I studied how clusters of
        gene duplicates evolved in the mammalian phylogeny, and the different ways in which gene
        clusters improve molecular diversity, with a specific interest in the evolution of pregnancy
        ications in studying preterm birth in humans. (and taught taught classes on
        Latin American food at the University)
      </.milestone_card>
      <.milestone_card
        image={~p"/images/japan.jpg"}
        image_alt="Nice garden afternoon in Osaka"
        title="SPDR Postdoctoral fellow"
        subtitle="RIKEN. Japan"
      >
        In my postdoc I moved to the
        <.link
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
          href="https://riken.jp"
        >
          RIKEN
        </.link>
        institute in Japan. At the
        <.link
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
          href="https://www.bdr.riken.jp/en/research/labs/kuraku-s/index.html"
        >
          Laboratory for Phyloinformatics
        </.link>
        at the
        <.link href="https://www.bdr.riken.jp/en/index.html">
          RIKEN Center for Biosystems Dynamics Research
        </.link>
        I developed computational tools to study the evolution of gene families in sharks, a basal. Then,
        as an
        <.link
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
          href="https://www.riken.jp/en/careers/programs/spdr/"
        >
          SPDR
        </.link>
        recipient, I worked in the
        <.link
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
          href="https://www.riken.jp/en/research/labs/ims/cell_conv/"
        >
          Laboratory for Advanced genomics Circuit
        </.link>
        at the
        <.link
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
          href="https://www.riken.jp/en/research/labs/ims/"
        >
          Center for Integrative Medical Sciences
        </.link>
        at <.link
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="link link-primary"
          href="http://www.riken.jp/en"
        >RIKEN</.link>, I developed data analysis and visualization
        applications to study chromatin dynamics in an evolutionary context.
      </.milestone_card>
    </div>
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold pt-8 pb-4">Development Skills</h2>
      <p class="pb-6">
        During this journey, I have collected some cool tools. Check them out!
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <.skill_card
          :for={set <- @skill_sets}
          title={set.area}
          icon={set.icon}
          skills={set.skills}
        />
      </div>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold pt-8 pb-4">Back to the real world</h2>

      <p class="pb-6">
        After years in academia, I moved into industry, where genomics meets the real world.
      </p>
      <ol class="ms-6 flex flex-col gap-10 border-s-2 border-primary/25">
        <.timeline_item
          title="Genomic and Data Analytics Core (GEDAC)"
          icon="hero-cloud"
          badges={["Singapore"]}
          highlights={["Team leadership", "Cloud infrastructure", "Genomics at scale"]}
        >
          After my post-doctoral fellowship at
          <.link
            href="https://www.riken.jp/en/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="link link-primary"
          >
            RIKEN
          </.link>
          in Japan, I started my professional career as a bioinformatician and computational biologist.
          At the
          <.link
            href="https://www.gedac.org/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="link link-primary"
          >
            Genomic and Data Analytics Core
          </.link>
          of the
          <.link
            href="https://csi.nus.edu.sg"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="link link-primary"
          >
            Cancer Sciences Institute
          </.link>
          (<.link
            href="https://nus.edu.sg"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="link link-primary"
          >National University of Singapore</.link>), I led a team of
          scientists and software developers to build the cloud infrastructure the institute needed
          to run genomic analytical pipelines at scale, work that has made a positive impact in the
          scientific community by letting researchers easily run genomic workflows in a cost-effective
          way from an intuitive interface.
        </.timeline_item>
        <.timeline_item
          title="Senior Bioinformatics Engineer · Lifebit"
          icon="hero-briefcase"
          badges={["Singapore"]}
          highlights={["Client liaison", "Deployment & maintenance", "Stakeholder communication"]}
        >
          Then, as a Senior Bioinformatics Engineer at <.link
            href="https://lifebit.ai"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="link link-primary"
          >Lifebit</.link>, my mission was to be the touch point with our clients in Singapore: communicating and
          developing technical insights to deploy and maintain the bioinformatics tools made by the
          company, with a high degree of communication between stakeholders at the client's
          organization and developers of Lifebit, to translate the needs of the clients into
          technical and scientific products.
        </.timeline_item>
        <.timeline_item
          title="Senior Computational Biologist · Paratus Sciences"
          icon="hero-beaker"
          badges={["Current"]}
          highlights={[
            "Drug target discovery",
            "Machine learning",
            "Phylogenetics",
            "Web technologies"
          ]}
        >
          Now, as a senior computational biologist at <.link
            href="https://paratussciences.com"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="link link-primary"
          >Paratus Sciences</.link>, I am busy deploying tools and original research to accelerate our drug target discovery
          engine. By combining machine learning, evolutionary biology, web technologies, and
          phylogenetics, I am empowering my team to push the limits of our discovery pipeline.
        </.timeline_item>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
